// Entity attributes: the leading `@[...]` marker attaches typed metadata to a
// declaration without changing what the declaration *is*
// (proposal-attributes.md §2). Attributes stack — one item takes several — and
// each carries a payload the ordinary checker types against its schema: `doc`
// wants a `String`, `deprecated` wants a record `#{ since : String, note :
// String }`. Attribute typing *is* ordinary value typing, no new rule.
//
// The attributes are inert: they live in a side table keyed by the item, never
// in its core-IR term, so `square`'s content-address is unchanged by adding,
// editing, or removing them (proposal-attributes.md §4.2, the `wyrd-q5r0`
// default). This is the canonical first read for the marker.
//
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: square
//@ expect-attribute: doc
//@ expect-attribute: deprecated
@[doc("Squares its argument.")]
@[deprecated(#{ since = "0.2", note = "use square_checked" })]
def square(x: Integer) -> F Integer {
  ret (x * x)
}
